# ==============================================================
# Public / private split for bioinformatics-research
# See CLASSIFICATION.md for the rationale behind every rule.
#
# Rule of thumb: anything that resolves to an INDIVIDUAL SAMPLE
# (per-sample x per-CpG values) stays private. Aggregates that
# collapse across samples are public.
# ==============================================================

# ---------- PRIVATE: individual-level methylation data ----------
# 380,355 CpGs x 53 samples of per-person flag calls.
# De-identified as N1..N53 / T1..T53, but still individual-level
# genomic data derived from controlled TCGA source files.
Results/Task13_Normal_selfref_flags.csv
Results/Task13_Normal_extref_flags.csv
Results/Task13_Tumor_selfref_flags.csv
Results/Task13_Tumor_extref_flags.csv
Results/Task13_FullFlagMatrix.xlsx
Results/Task17_Chr22_BiologicalValidation_Normal_100CpGs.csv

# Reference quantile tables: the P0.00001 / N0.00001 columns are
# effectively the max/min beta of a single individual per CpG, so
# these leak individual values despite looking like aggregates.
Results/experiment7_ref_normal.rds
Results/experiment7_ref_tumor.rds
*.rds

# ---------- PRIVATE: source and third-party reference data ----------
# Not ours to redistribute; lives on leap2 under another lab's home.
Data/
*.tar.gz
*.rda

# ---------- Python bytecode ----------
# Scripts/docx_kit.py is imported by build_meeting_doc_sep03.py, which
# makes CPython write a __pycache__ alongside it.
Scripts/__pycache__/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# ---------- PRIVATE: R session state ----------
.RData
.Rhistory
.RDataTmp
.Rproj.user/

# ---------- OS noise ----------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---------- Third-party vendored package ----------
# OutlierMeth is GPL-2 code by Downs & Cope (JHMI), cloned from
# github.com/bdowns4/OutlierMeth. It carries its own .git, which
# would otherwise land in our history as a broken submodule.
# Tracked as a documented dependency instead - see CLASSIFICATION.md.
Packages/OutlierMeth/.git/

# ---------- PRIVATE: site-level drill-down tables ----------
# The Task 18-21 "detail" and "cluster" outputs name a cgID, a
# genomic position AND a sample, and carry that sample's beta value.
# That is individual-level data at identified sites - the same class
# as the flag matrices above, just narrower. The per-sample COUNT
# tables (StateSummary, ContraryCounts, Concordance, SampleBurden,
# ScaleComparison, ContraryDrivers, ExtFlagMagnitude) carry no
# genomic coordinates and stay public, consistent with the Task 13/14
# sample summaries. See CLASSIFICATION.md.
Results/*ContraryDetail*

# Per-SITE reconstructed external thresholds. flagMeth sets +1 iff
# beta > P, so bracketing P between the highest unflagged and lowest
# flagged beta at a named CpG bounds two individuals' values there.
# Same class as the experiment7_ref_*.rds threshold tables above; the
# per-STATE aggregate version (Task22_Chr22_ThresholdGeometry_*) stays
# public because it collapses across sites.
Results/Task29_Window100_SiteThresholdGeometry.csv
Results/*ContraryFlagDetail*
Results/*TopSampleDetail*
Results/*_Cluster_*

# ---------- Safety net ----------
# Any future per-sample flag matrix should be private by default.
Results/*_flags.csv
Results/*FullFlagMatrix*
.venv/

# ---------- PRIVATE: Task 36 top-site drill-down ----------
# Per-sample betas, flags and ranks at named CpGs, and a site summary
# whose Min/Max columns are single individuals' values. The Zhou
# manifests and the hg38 sequence cache sit under Data/ (already ignored).
Results/Task36_*Detail*
Results/Task36_TopSites_Summary.csv

# The Sep 15 report quotes per-sample beta values at named CpGs.
sep15.docx

# ---------- PRIVATE: single individuals' values in Tasks 36, 39, 44 ----------
# Task 36 console log: prints single samples' betas at named CpGs, the
# same content as the Task 36 detail tables above.
Scripts/Task36.TopSiteDeepDive.Sep15.2026.Rout
# Task 36 figures. Fig13 plots every sample's beta at 12 named CpGs,
# extremes included; Fig14 and Fig19 label named samples' betas at named
# CpGs.
Results/Fig13_TopSites_RawBeta.png
Results/Fig14_Pair_Neighbourhood.png
Results/Fig19_Pair2_Neighbourhood.png
# RRBS (18 patients, another lab's data): the per-site summary's Min and
# Max are single individuals' values at named sites, as for Task 36.
Results/Task39_RRBS_SiteSummary.csv.gz
# Fig21 plots all 18 individuals' values at six real RRBS sites. The
# sites are not named, but each can be found from the public per-site
# medians, so it is treated like the site summary (a borderline call).
Results/Fig21_RRBS_StateDefinitions.png

# ---------- Raw GEO and CNGB metadata dumps (Task 68) ----------
# Full GEO sample records include per-person traits (for example height
# and weight in GSE186888) that no analysis needs. The run reports and
# manifests derived from them are committed instead.
Results/Task68_Metadata/*.soft
Results/Task68_Metadata/*.html
